# rofi -dmenu for hyprland, on a quickshell menu (Dmenu.qml): the rows come
# on stdin, this prints the picked one, nothing and exit 1 on esc. it takes
# the rofi flags the tab switcher and scripts use, the rest is ignored.
# pango markup in the rows (-markup-rows) is dropped, a <span> starts the
# dim column. default.nix installs it as hypr-dmenu
#   hypr-dmenu [-p prompt] [-selected-row N] [-format i|s] [-markup-rows]
#   hypr-dmenu --check    exit 0 while quickshell runs

prompt="" selected=0 format=s markup=0
while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case $1 in
    --check) exec qs -c hyprland ipc show >/dev/null 2>&1 ;;
    -p) prompt=${2:-}; shift ;;
    -selected-row) selected=${2:-0}; shift ;;
    -format) format=${2:-s}; shift ;;
    -markup-rows) markup=1 ;;
    -theme | -theme-str | -scroll-method | -mesg | -l | -lines) shift ;;
  esac
  shift
done

dir=${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/hypr-dmenu
mkdir -p "$dir"
rows=$dir/$$
trap 'rm -f "$rows"' EXIT
cat >"$rows"

# the wait is up before the menu can answer
{
  sleep 0.2
  qs -c hyprland ipc call dmenu ask "$rows" "$prompt" "$selected" "$markup" >/dev/null
} &
i=$(qs -c hyprland ipc wait dmenu answered)

case $i in "" | *[!0-9]*) exit 1 ;; esac
if [ "$format" = i ]; then
  printf '%s\n' "$i"
else
  sed -n "$((i + 1))p" "$rows"
fi
